# Everything `npm run fetch:agi` and `npm run fetch:sci` write.
#
# `games/*` hides a game's data files, and the names negated under it are the
# exception: a game folder's documentation is tracked and its data never is
# (ADR 0031). `docs/processes/verifying-version-support.md` is where the
# consequence — CI runs on a synthetic fixture — is described.
#
# Git does not look inside an excluded directory, so `!games/*/README.md` on
# its own would never fire: the directory is excluded before the file is ever
# considered. Re-including the directories and then excluding their contents is
# what makes the three negations below reachable.
games/*
!games/README.md
!games/*/
games/*/*
!games/*/README.md
!games/*/image.jpg
!games/*/image.png

# A Sandcastle run's own prompt, which is a local file rather than a record.
#
# `.sandcastle/main.ts` resolves a run name to `prompt-<name>.md`, and those
# used to be tracked — nineteen of them, one per job, every one the prompt of
# something that had already shipped. A prompt is written against measurements
# taken the day it is launched, so a committed one is a snapshot of a tree that
# no longer exists, and reviewing a pull request meant reading one.
#
# `prompt.md` is the exception and is tracked, because it is not a job: it is
# the worked example of what a prompt here has to contain.
.sandcastle/prompt-*.md
!.sandcastle/prompt.md

# Rust build output and the generated WASM package
target/
engine/pkg/
/.claude/worktrees/

# The htdemucs export (tools/htdemucs-onnx/): its venv and what it writes.
# Model weights are for personal use only and never committed (ADR 0005).
tools/htdemucs-onnx/.venv
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pth
*.th
*.onnx
*.ort

# The model `pnpm htdemucs:export` writes by default. Its weights are for
# personal use only (ADR 0005): never commit or publish it.
/model/
